<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2629" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰπος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰπύς</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>height, steep</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				285
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				309
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς αἶπος ὁδοιπορῆσαι,
				ἰέναι</span> to toil up-<i>hill</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Morb.</u>
				2.51
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				70
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς αἶπος ἔρχεται</span>,
			metaph. of a difficult task, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				500
			</span></i>: hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἶ</span>. (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆπος</span>
			 )<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ἐκβαλὼν ὁδοῦ</span>, i.e. the
				<i>weariness</i> of the ascent (expl. by <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάματος</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				851
			</span></i> (unless <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκβαλών</span>
			= 'forgetting').</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
